From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:49:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a plugin model that refuses temperature is asked
 without it, relayed or translated (#2492)

What changed: the plugin host carries a model's temperature where it is
said - the config model's temperature (Factory 0.1.31's configModels,
plugins#154), models.dev's own, or a models hook's model field - into
plugin.Model and pluginCatalog's catalog model, where
RejectsTemperature reads it as it reads a built-in's. A Chat or
Responses request relayed as it came to a model whose list refuses
temperature and top_p now leaves them out (passthrough), as the
translation of one (build) already did. A model nothing says so of
keeps what the client sent. OpenCode's capabilities.temperature is not
read: its false is what it reads a models.dev silence as, not a refusal
said.

Docs: the sampling row of gateway-routing, and provider-plugins' new
"A plugin model's sampling".

Run at ea3dee96 + this change, sandbox HOME:
go test -tags nogui -p 2 -run TestPluginModelRefusingTemperature
./internal/gateway/ - red at ea3dee96 without this change (the plugin's
fetch got temperature 0.7, top_p 0.9 relayed, temperature 0.7
translated; the model that says nothing keeps them), green with it;
ablation removed the four product files and went red the same way.
go test -tags nogui -p 2 -timeout 45m ./internal/gateway/ ok (291s);
go test -tags nogui -p 2 ./internal/plugin/ ok; -run
'TestRejectsTemperature|TestPluginModel|TestPluginCatalog|PluginParity|TestPlugin'
./internal/provider/ ok; -run
'TestSampling|TestUpstreamBytes|TestPassthrough|TestRelay'
./internal/gateway/ ok.
gofmt -l internal/ clean; go vet ./... (darwin, the
trayimage_darwin.go cgo warning as before), GOOS=linux go vet -tags
